      <p>Checked on 17 and 18 October 2026. Measurements come from PostgreSQL 18.6 with a 16 MB pool on one laptop, and show which pages stayed cached, not performance. The sizing table and the warm-up estimate are arithmetic from stated assumptions. MySQL and SQL Server weren’t run; their behaviour is as documented.</p>
